# Spotler Design System Usage Skill

## Purpose
Use this Skill when designing Spotler interfaces in Figma Make.

The attached **Spotler Design System Kit** is the visual source of truth. Use the Kit components, variants, variables, and tokens first. Do not invent new UI unless the Kit has no suitable component.

## Core rule
Product Skill decides **what the feature does**.  
Design System Kit decides **how it looks**.  
This Skill decides **how to use the Kit correctly**.

## Always do
- Use existing Kit components first
- Use component tokens before foundation tokens
- Keep spacing, typography, radius, and colour from the Kit
- Include hover, focus, selected, disabled, error, empty, and loading states where relevant
- Use accessible labels and visible focus states
- Use real Spotler patterns for forms, tables, dashboards, modals, cards, and setup flows

## Avoid
- Inventing new components
- Hardcoded colours or spacing
- Generic SaaS styling
- Ignoring states
- Using colour alone for status
- Replacing tables with cards when data is tabular
- Using modals for complex full-page workflows

## When designing
First check the Kit for:
- Layout pattern
- Existing component
- Component variant
- Token/state rules
- Accessibility expectations

## Example prompt
Using the Spotler Design System Usage Skill and the Spotler CRM Product Context Skill, design a contact detail page using only components and patterns from the Spotler Design System Kit.
